Package: keyway-dev-env
Version: 0.1.0
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: arthurffht <arthurffht@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/arthurffht/keyway
Depends: build-essential,
 pkg-config,
 git,
 jq,
 meson,
 ninja-build,
 just,
 gh,
 rustup,
 libglib2.0-dev,
 libgtk-4-dev,
 libadwaita-1-dev,
 blueprint-compiler,
 gettext,
 desktop-file-utils,
 appstream,
 reuse,
 nodejs,
 npm,
 podman,
 uidmap,
 passt,
 catatonit,
 python3-dbusmock,
 mutter-dev-bin,
 sysprof,
 hyperfine,
 valgrind,
 shellcheck
Description: Host development environment for Keyway
 Metapackage that pulls in every host tool Keyway development needs
 (docs/PLAN.md §30.1). Removing it with
 "apt purge keyway-dev-env && apt autoremove --purge" removes exactly
 the packages it brought in.
 .
 Debian packaging tools (debhelper, dh-cargo, devscripts, lintian) are
 deliberately excluded: dh-cargo conflicts with rustup, so packages are
 built inside containers instead.
